   "@id": "https://github.com/jmholton/phenix_user_solvent#quote-c15",
   "@type": "Item",
   "format": "text/plain",
   "content": "The flat mask contributes nothing above 3 Å.",
   "isContainedBy": "https://github.com/jmholton/phenix_user_solvent",
   "title": "phenix_user_solvent README, Iterative workflow"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:q3",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Where does the flat binary bulk-solvent mask fail to describe crystal solvent?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Most refinement programs fill the region outside the atomic model with constant electron density. The paper lists the ways this assumption departs from real solvent."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Purpose; Background, paragraphs 2-4",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2053273324000299",
    "https://doi.org/10.1006/jmbi.1994.1633"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:q1",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Can phenix.refine use an externally computed bulk-solvent map in place of the flat mask?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Physically richer solvent models exist, but Phenix had no way to take them as input. The paper asks whether a small local change can add this."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Purpose; Background, paragraph 4",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444912001308"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:q2",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Does a user-supplied solvent map improve fit to the X-ray data compared with the flat mask?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Fit is measured by R-work and cross-validated R-free on a high-resolution test structure."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent: Effect on refinement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:q4",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - How can a 48-member protein ensemble be refined and validated with a structured solvent model?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The test case uses a large multiconformer ensemble, which strains standard validation tools."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent: Effect on refinement; Table 1",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.3330"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c1",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Inaccurate solvent modeling is a major driver of the gap between refinement R values and data quality",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Crystals are 20-90% solvent by volume, about 50% on average, and all of it scatters X-rays. Solvent is still modeled with crude approximations, which leaves a large R-factor gap."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Purpose; Background, paragraphs 1 and 3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/2me0-hd96#quote-c1",
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-2836%2868%2990205-2",
    "https://doi.org/10.1021/ci500662d",
    "https://doi.org/10.1111/febs.12922"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c2",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - A flat mask cannot represent structured density from waters, ions, lipids and buffer components",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The flat model assumes disordered solvent is spread evenly through the non-masked part of the asymmetric unit. Real solvent has structure that this ignores."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Background, paragraphs 2-3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.4909",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444900014608"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c3",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The binary mask treats the unoccupied fraction of partially occupied atoms as vacuum",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Any atom with occupancy below 1 is fully excluded from the solvent mask. This affects multiconformer models and partially occupied waters, and adding many low-occupancy waters to compensate inflates parameters and destabilizes refinement."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Background, paragraph 3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.7554/elife.103797",
    "https://doi.org/10.7554/elife.90606",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2059798323002498",
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/bs.mie.2023.06.009"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c4",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Sharp mask edges and solvent assigned to unmodeled regions leave systematic errors in difference maps",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Fourier ripples from the mask boundary appear at high resolution. Solvent density placed over unmodeled parts of the model smears density and lowers peak heights, which Polder maps can correct but refinement programs rarely use."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Background, paragraph 3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2059798316018210",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444910031045"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c5",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The mosaic bulk-solvent model improves on the flat mask but keeps the binary-boundary approximation",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The mosaic model gives each isolated solvent region its own occupancy. It still treats solvent as a structureless continuum and does not fix the partial-occupancy problem."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Background, paragraph 4",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.4909"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c6",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Physically based solvent models exist but have been hard to integrate into Phenix",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "MD simulations, 3D-RISM, holographic methods such as EDEN and neural networks can all predict solvent density. Getting their output into standard refinement has been the practical barrier."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Purpose; Background, paragraph 4; 'A user-supplied bulk solvent map can replace the flat mask', paragraph 1",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0070869",
    "https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jcim.5c01063",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444912001308",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2059798322011871",
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1402",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s010876739601584x"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c7",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Other refinement programs already accept a precomputed solvent or partial-structure contribution",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Buster, Refmac5, SHELXL, PLATON, AMBER and X-PLOR/CNS allow this. Refmac5 accepts up to five partial structures through FPART/PHIPART columns."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. 'The flat-mask bulk-solvent model is an approximation of structured solvent', paragraph 3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1006/jmbi.1994.1633",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444904016427",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444911001314",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2053229614024218",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2053229614024929",
    "https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jcim.3c01531"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c8",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - A compact local patch lets phenix.refine use user-supplied solvent structure factors as F_mask",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The user's amplitude and phase columns replace the flat-mask F_mask, and k_mask is still fit analytically per resolution bin, so the map can be on any scale. The map is held fixed during refinement and fully replaces the mask."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. 'A user-supplied bulk solvent map can replace the flat mask'; Scaling and treatment during refinement",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444912001308",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444913000462",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2059798323004825",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2059798319011471",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s090744491102258x"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c10",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Solvent MTZ files prepared for Refmac can be used in Phenix without relabeling",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The default column labels are FPART and PHIPART, following the Refmac convention. If the experimental MTZ already holds these columns, no separate file is needed."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. 'A user-supplied bulk solvent map can replace the flat mask', paragraph 2; Input specification",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444911001314"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c9",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The supplied map must be carried through outlier rejection or it is silently discarded",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Each outlier-rejection step rebuilds the f_model manager. Without propagating the map through select(), Phenix recomputes the flat mask and the supplied map has no effect on the result."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Reflection outlier rejection"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c16",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The patch does not support joint X-ray/neutron refinement, and twin refinement is untested",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "These are the two limitations the authors state for the current patch."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. 'A user-supplied bulk solvent map can replace the flat mask', paragraph 2"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c11",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Replacing the flat mask with a physically based solvent map lowers cross-validated R-free",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "For the 1AHO test case, both an MD-derived map in Phenix and 3D-RISM solvent in Table 1 gave lower R-free than flat bulk solvent."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent: Effect on refinement; Table 1"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c12",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The R-free gain reflects a better solvent model rather than overfitting",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Free-flagged reflections were excluded from all map editing, so the R-free change is cross-validated. Model geometry did not change and the R-free/R-work gap stayed small."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent: Effect on refinement, paragraph 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/355472a0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c13",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The size of the improvement will depend on resolution, solvent content and map quality",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The authors present 1AHO as a single test case, not a general benchmark. Its high-resolution, ambient-temperature data and nearly pure-water solvent make it a favorable system."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent, paragraph 1; text after Table 1"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c14",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Ensemble modeling gave larger R-free gains than solvent map editing",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "In the 1AHO series, density editing of the solvent map contributed small R-free gains compared with moving to a multiconformer ensemble."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Text after Table 1; Table 1"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c15",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Per-bin k_mask in Phenix corrects resolution-dependent miscalibration of MD solvent maps",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "A single global B-factor applied to the MD map blurs it and suppresses its high-resolution content. Fitting k_mask per resolution bin restores that content, so fewer explicit waters are needed to patch the deficit."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "phenix_user_solvent README, github.com/jmholton/phenix_user_solvent. README: Iterative workflow",
   "references": [
    "https://github.com/jmholton/phenix_user_solvent#quote-c15"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c17",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Iterating refinement and solvent density editing further lowers R-free",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "After refinement with the supplied map, remaining Fo-Fc features in the solvent are treated as missing structure and added back to the map. The README describes repeating this until solvent peaks fall below about 3 sigma."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "phenix_user_solvent README, github.com/jmholton/phenix_user_solvent. README: Example; Iterative workflow"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:c18",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Supercell ensembles refine as stably as single-ASU models and resolve non-bonded ambiguities",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The 48-member ensemble was refined as a 2x2x3 supercell with full-occupancy copies. It was condensed to one ASU with 48 altlocs only for this demonstration, because supercell refinement is not widely adopted."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent: Effect on refinement, paragraph 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.3330"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:e1",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - MD-derived map lowered R-free from 0.1473 to 0.1092 and R-work from 0.1278 to 0.0928",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Same starting ensemble, data and three macro-cycles in phenix.refine; only the solvent source differed. Part of the R-work gain is expected because the map was edited against working-set difference density."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent: Effect on refinement, results table",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.2210/pdb1aho/pdb"
   ],
   "sourceDocument": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/2me0-hd96"
   ],
   "observationOriginActivity": "bsm:s1"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:e2",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - Bond r.m.s.d. was 0.007 Å in both the flat-mask and MD-map runs",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Model geometry was essentially unchanged by the switch in solvent source, and the R-free/R-work gap remained small."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent: Effect on refinement, paragraph 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.2210/pdb1aho/pdb"
   ],
   "sourceDocument": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/2me0-hd96"
   ],
   "observationOriginActivity": "bsm:s1"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:e3",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - Flat bulk solvent gave R-free 0.1664; 3D-RISM solvent gave 0.1302",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Both runs used occupancy-refined waters. MolProbity scores were 2.94 for both."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Table 1, rows 2-3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.2210/pdb1aho/pdb"
   ],
   "sourceDocument": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/2me0-hd96"
   ],
   "observationOriginActivity": "bsm:s2"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:e4",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - map_touchup density editing lowered R-free only from 0.1181 to 0.1161",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "This step followed the 48-copy supercell refinement with MD average solvent, ordered waters and watershed, which itself reached R-free 0.1181 from 0.1239 for the 2-8 conformer model."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Table 1, rows 4-6",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.2210/pdb1aho/pdb"
   ],
   "sourceDocument": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/2me0-hd96"
   ],
   "observationOriginActivity": "bsm:s2"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:e5",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - msander plus Refmac5 supercell refinement reached R-free 0.1107 with MolProbity 1.06",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The single-ASU phenix.refine run with 48 altlocs reached R-free 0.1089, but MolProbity crashed on it."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Table 1, rows 7-8",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.3330",
    "https://doi.org/10.2210/pdb1aho/pdb"
   ],
   "sourceDocument": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/2me0-hd96"
   ],
   "observationOriginActivity": "bsm:s2"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:e6",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - Flat-mask k_mask was 0.00 above 3 Å; MD-map k_mask was 1.12 to 1.45 there",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "At low resolution (14-6.7 Å) k_mask was 0.33 for the flat mask and 1.05 for the MD map. Values above 1 at high resolution indicate the global B-factor had undersold the map amplitude."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "phenix_user_solvent README, github.com/jmholton/phenix_user_solvent. README: Iterative workflow, k_mask table",
