  {
   "@id": "bsm:p1",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Protocol",
    "mira:Protocol"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "PRO - Apply the three phenix_user_solvent patches to a Phenix installation",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Patch f_model.py, phenix/programs/phenix_refine.py and __init__.params under site-packages (Phenix 2.x) or modules/ (Phenix 1.21 and earlier). Other files named phenix_refine.py must not be patched."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Installation; Modified source files"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:p2",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Protocol",
    "mira:Protocol"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "PRO - phenix.refine with refinement.input.bulk_solvent_map",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Pass file_name, amplitudes_label and phases_label. The 1AHO runs used three macro-cycles refining individual sites and ADPs."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Input specification; Map ingestion and indexing; Effect on refinement",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444912001308"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:p3",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Protocol",
    "mira:Protocol"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "PRO - MD-derived solvent map with density editing",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Average solvent density from an AMBER trajectory with crystal packing, then add Fo-Fc difference features back into the map with free-flagged reflections excluded. The ensemble was optimized with msander, ramping the X-ray term while lowering temperature."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Generating the solvent map",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jcim.5c01063",
    "https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jcim.3c01531",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2059798322011871",
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1402",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/355472a0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:p4",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Protocol",
    "mira:Protocol"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "PRO - Iterative refine, inspect and density-edit cycle",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Refine with the user map for 3-10 cycles, export FMASK and K_MASK, add positive solvent blobs to the solvent MTZ and repeat. Stop when the k_mask profile stabilizes and solvent Fo-Fc peaks fall below about 3 sigma."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "phenix_user_solvent README, github.com/jmholton/phenix_user_solvent. README: Iterative workflow"
  },
  {
   "@id": "bsm:p5",
   "@type": [
    "bsm:schema-Protocol",
    "mira:Protocol"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "PRO - 48-copy supercell ensemble refinement",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Data and solvent structure factors re-indexed by 2h,2k,3l, the cell enlarged 2x2x3 in P212121, and filled with 48 full-occupancy copies of the monomer."
   },
   "creator": "bsm:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Holton and Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/2me0-hd96. Example of AMBER bulk solvent: Effect on refinement, paragraph 2"
  },
